  "answer": "Based on UNHCR's Global Trends 2020 report, the top 5 countries with the most internally displaced people in 2020 were:\n\n1. **Colombia** — 8.3 million IDPs\n2. **Syria** — 6.7 million IDPs\n3. **Democratic Republic of the Congo** — 5.2 million IDPs\n4. **Yemen** — 4.0 million IDPs\n5. **Somalia** — 3.0 million IDPs\n\nUsing World Bank / ILO modelled estimates for employment in agriculture (% of total employment) in 2020:\n\n| Country | Employment in agriculture (% of total employment) |\n|---------|---------------------------------------------------|\n| **Colombia** | **15.81%** |\n| Syria | 16.91% |\n| Somalia | 30.05% |\n| Yemen | 32.06% |\n| DRC | 60.93% |\n\n**Colombia had the lowest percentage of people employed in agriculture in 2020 at 15.81%.**",
